# --------------------------------------------------
# Canonical development-container checksums.
#
# Records SHA-256 values for Linux artifacts downloaded directly by the
# Dockerfile. A checksum identifies the expected contents of a downloaded file.
# The build rejects the file if its contents do not match the committed hash.
#
# This is not a checksum list for every dependency in the container. Container
# images and Features are pinned in Dockerfile and devcontainer-lock.json.
# Tools installed through mise use mise.lock and its native lock sidecars.
#
# Entries use the canonical sha256sum text format: a 64-character digest, two
# spaces, then the artifact filename.
# --------------------------------------------------

# --------------------------
# Mise checksums
#
# These two entries pin the mise executable used to bootstrap tool installation.
# The Dockerfile reads MISE_VERSION from versions.env and downloads the binary
# for the target architecture. Docker calls these architectures amd64 and arm64,
# while mise calls its release binaries linux-x64 and linux-arm64.
#
# The build checks the selected binary against its hash below before installing
# it. It does not download replacement hashes or verify a publisher signature
# during the build. This keeps the committed checksum as the build's reference.
#
# When updating mise, the bootstrap updater downloads the publisher's release
# manifest and its .minisig signature. Minisign verifies that signature against
# the publisher key pinned in scripts/node/bin/update-mise-bootstrap.js. This
# proves that the manifest was signed by the holder of that key, rather than merely
# trusting a checksum downloaded alongside the binary. Key changes need review.
#
# Run the following command from the repository root to update the bootstrap
# version, both hashes, the minimum mise version and the CI bootstrap pin together.
# Replace VERSION with the desired release number without a leading v.
# bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --mise VERSION
#
# Keep these entries in the standard sha256sum format. The updater preserves
# this explanation and updates the release-manifest URL along with the hashes.
#
# The publisher's checksum manifest for the committed release is available at
# https://github.com/jdx/mise/releases/download/v2026.9.18/SHASUMS256.txt
# --------------------------

# https://github.com/jdx/mise/releases/download/v2026.9.18/SHASUMS256.txt
d24fe0bf7e613824ad99f7b8dac3f2b381a37b9f75f84dd250855217095a8de4  mise-v2026.9.18-linux-x64
2142433ae70decffc5fa24bd160e47931e33f55eb031d128beb97cbae634d168  mise-v2026.9.18-linux-arm64
